{"abstract":"Mesenchymal stromal cells (MSCs) are being tested in numerous clinical trials, yet the limited progression of these trials to advanced stages indicates unresolved translational challenges. Expanding MSCs is a critical step in most therapeutic applications, and bioreactor-based culture offers large-scale production compared to monolayer cultures. Nevertheless, since MSCs sense their microenvironment, it is crucial to understand how these systems affect their properties. We expanded human adipose-derived mesenchymal stromal cells (AD-MSCs) from the same donors in both small- and large-scale platforms. Bulk-RNA sequencing (RNA-seq) and mass spectrometry analysis demonstrated that small-scale culture had a broader range of differentially expressed genes (DEGs) and proteins within immunomodulatory, cell migration, and cell adhesion pathways. In contrast, the large-scale culture showed a lower amount of DEGs and proteins associated mainly with extracellular matrix synthesis. Our findings demonstrate that expansion platforms significantly impact MSCs’ properties, highlighting the need to optimize expansion conditions to obtain high cell yield without compromising MSCs’ attributes.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Galera, Marina Ramírez","Oikonomou, Athanasios","Elsborg, Jonas D.","Harth, Lisa","Fischer-Nielsen, Anne","Løvendorf, Marianne Bengtson","Dyring-Andersen, Beatrice","Iorio, Francesco","Fog, Lea Munthe","Woetmann, Anders","Svalgaard, Jesper Dyrendom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-819499"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Computational Biology Research Centre, Human Technopole","Fondazione Human Technopole"],"keyword":["Bioreactor","Cell expansion","Immunomodulation","MSCs","Transcriptomics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Celcore"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of cell culture transition on adipose derived mesenchymal stromal cells multi omics analysis of small vs large scale production","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.omtm.2025.101512","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-819499","identifier":[{"id":"105009437769","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-81449c79-bbd7-4424-b5b0-e2fec4552837"],"keyword":["AD-MSCs","MSCs","adipose-derived mesenchymal stromal cells","bioreactor","cell expansion","culture platform","immunomodulation","large-scale cell production","transcriptomics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-17CBF9A86E6B581F086477A500705DD5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/456083625/Impact_of_cell_culture_transition.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.omtm.2025.101512","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Skin Immunology Research Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"computational biology research centre human technopole","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Computational Biology Research Centre, Human Technopole","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Celcore"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"it","key":"fondazione human technopole","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fondazione Human Technopole","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marina Ramírez","key":"galerapau","last":"Galera","locid":"51a1f4a2-848d-4817-936a-adede4a4070f","name":"Galera, Marina Ramírez","orcid":"0000-0001-9797-8512","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Athanasios","key":"oikonomoupau","last":"Oikonomou","name":"Oikonomou, Athanasios","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas D.","key":"elsborgpau","last":"Elsborg","locid":"dbd544fa-a21d-4a87-b5ff-226aa2f424b6","name":"Elsborg, Jonas D.","orcid":"0000-0002-1506-4280","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lisa","key":"harthpau","last":"Harth","locid":"07113df3-377c-4814-8bd2-ca1ad73ad2fb","name":"Harth, Lisa","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anne","key":"fischernielsenpau","last":"Fischer-Nielsen","name":"Fischer-Nielsen, Anne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4 5","first":"Marianne Bengtson","key":"løvendorfpau","last":"Løvendorf","locid":"c2444ac6-8300-4e66-9b0a-c5a153a7ea30","name":"Løvendorf, Marianne Bengtson","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 1","first":"Beatrice","key":"dyringandersenpau","last":"Dyring-Andersen","locid":"8d2c8b9b-81bb-458e-aad4-4653e0ace0d6","name":"Dyring-Andersen, Beatrice","orcid":"0000-0002-3012-2645","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Francesco","key":"ioriopau","last":"Iorio","name":"Iorio, Francesco","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Lea Munthe","key":"fogpau","last":"Fog","name":"Fog, Lea Munthe","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"woetmannpau","last":"Woetmann","locid":"18df0978-d38c-4ffb-985d-b544e22fa387","name":"Woetmann, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-3008-735X","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jesper Dyrendom","key":"svalgaardpau","last":"Svalgaard","name":"Svalgaard, Jesper Dyrendom","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.omtm.2025.101512","issn":["23290501"],"issue":"3","journal":"Molecular Therapy Methods and Clinical Development","paperid":"101512","status":"p","title":"Molecular Therapy Methods and Clinical Development","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105009437769"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-81449c79-bbd7-4424-b5b0-e2fec4552837"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Impact of cell culture transition on adipose-derived mesenchymal stromal cells : Multi-omics analysis of small- vs large-scale production","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-819499","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Multiparty session types is a typing discipline used to write specifications, known as global types, for branching and recursive message-passing systems. A necessary operation on global types is projection to abstractions of local behaviour, called local types. Typically, this is a computable partial function that given a global type and a role erases all details irrelevant to this role. Computable projection functions in the literature are either unsound or too restrictive when dealing with recursion and branching. Recent work has taken a more general approach to projection defining it as a coinductive, but not computable, relation. Our work defines a new computable projection function that is sound and complete with respect to its coinductive counterpart and, hence, equally expressive. All results have been mechanised in the Coq proof assistant.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Tirore, Dawit","Bengtson, Jesper","Carbone, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695307"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Coq","Mechanisation","Projection","Session types"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a sound and complete projection for global types","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2023/18403/pdf/LIPIcs-ITP-2023-28.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695307","identifier":[{"id":"85168768440","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ed2c6e7a-d23b-4243-8a79-703d470a4895"],"keyword":["Coq","Mechanisation","Projection","Session types"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-5CCB516C5885FDDD1B2BA73762D97C9B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2023/18403/pdf/LIPIcs-ITP-2023-28.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2023/18403/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dawit","key":"tirorepau","last":"Tirore","locid":"12df9187-47b5-4d7e-87f5-9089a3d229c1","name":"Tirore, Dawit","orcid":"0000-0002-1997-5161","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"bengtsonpau","last":"Bengtson","locid":"b2b68ce2-6257-45bf-ab48-dc17d05c885e","name":"Bengtson, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18688969"],"journal":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","status":"p","title":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","volume":"268"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85168768440"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ed2c6e7a-d23b-4243-8a79-703d470a4895"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Sound and Complete Projection for Global Types","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695307","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Message passing is a useful abstraction for implementing concurrent programs. For real-world systems, however, it is often combined with other programming and concurrency paradigms, such as higher-order functions, mutable state, shared-memory concurrency, and locks. We present Actris: a logic for proving functional correctness of programs that use a combination of the aforementioned features. Actris combines the power of modern concurrent separation logics with a first-class protocol mechanism—based on session types— for reasoning about message passing in the presence of other concurrency paradigms. We show that Actris provides a suitable level of abstraction by proving functional correctness of a variety of examples, including a channel-based merge sort, a channel-based load-balancing mapper, and a variant of the map-reduce model, using concise specifications. While Actris was already presented in a conference paper (POPL’20), this paper expands the prior presentation significantly. Moreover, it extends Actris to Actris 2.0 with a notion of subprotocols—based on session-type subtyping—that permits additional flexibility when composing channel endpoints, and that takes full advantage of the asynchronous semantics of message passing in Actris. Soundness of Actris 2.0 is proven using a model of its protocol mechanism in the Iris framework. We have mechanised the theory of Actris, together with custom tactics, as well as all examples in the paper, in the Coq proof assistant.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hinrichsen, Jonas Kastberg","Bengtson, Jesper","Krebbers, Robbert"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-260887"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Radboud University Nijmegen"],"keyword":["Actor model","Concurrency","Iris","Message passing","Session types"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"actris 000000000002 000000000000 asynchronous session type based reasoning in separation logic","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.46298/lmcs-18(2:16)2022","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-260887","identifier":[{"id":"85134740099","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e66e1855-83f7-4b84-bdfc-3f410a41b164"],"keyword":["Iris","Message passing","actor model","concurrency","session types"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-995A6F59DA758D3AB4EB903335582547"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.46298/lmcs-18(2:16)2022","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"radboud university nijmegen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Radboud University Nijmegen","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Kastberg","key":"hinrichsenpau","last":"Hinrichsen","locid":"47107d73-8750-4515-ba0f-33c7ba993099","name":"Hinrichsen, Jonas Kastberg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"bengtsonpau","last":"Bengtson","name":"Bengtson, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Robbert","key":"krebberspau","last":"Krebbers","name":"Krebbers, Robbert","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.46298/lmcs-18(2:16)2022","issn":["18605974"],"issue":"2","journal":"Logical Methods in Computer Science","publisher":"Logical Methods in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Logical Methods in Computer Science","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134740099"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e66e1855-83f7-4b84-bdfc-3f410a41b164"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"ACTRIS 2.0 : ASYNCHRONOUS SESSION-TYPE BASED REASONING IN SEPARATION LOGIC","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-260887","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Session types—a family of type systems for message-passing concurrency—have been subject to many extensions, where each extension comes with a separate proof of type safety. These extensions cannot be readily combined, and their proofs of type safety are generally not machine checked, making their correctness less trustworthy. We overcome these shortcomings with a semantic approach to binary asynchronous affine session types, by developing a logical relations model in Coq using the Iris program logic. We demonstrate the power of our approach by combining various forms of polymorphism and recursion, asynchronous subtyping, references, and locks/mutexes. As an additional benefit of the semantic approach, we demonstrate how to manually prove typing judgements of racy, but safe, programs that cannot be type checked using only the rules of the type system.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hinrichsen, Jonas Kastberg","Louwrink, Daniël","Krebbers, Robbert","Bengtson, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382729"],"event":{"acronym":"CPP","title":"ACM SIGPLAN International Conference on Certified Programs and Proofs"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology","Radboud University Nijmegen","University of Amsterdam"],"keyword":["Coq","Iris","Message passing","Semantic typing","Separation logic","Session types"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"machine checked semantic session typing","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3437992.3439914","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382729","identifier":[{"id":"85100539579","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-618f45a0-50de-43b2-a610-fe8b52212bdd"],"keyword":["Coq","Iris","Message passing","Semantic typing","Separation logic","Session types"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A0CECA95A56FA5B289E244A38EE66E7C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85827344/Machine_Checked_Semantic_Session_Typing.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3437992.3439914","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"university of amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Amsterdam","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Delft University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"radboud university nijmegen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Radboud University Nijmegen","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Kastberg","key":"hinrichsenpau","last":"Hinrichsen","name":"Hinrichsen, Jonas Kastberg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniël","key":"louwrinkpau","last":"Louwrink","name":"Louwrink, Daniël","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Robbert","key":"krebberspau","last":"Krebbers","name":"Krebbers, Robbert","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"bengtsonpau","last":"Bengtson","locid":"b2b68ce2-6257-45bf-ab48-dc17d05c885e","name":"Bengtson, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3437992.3439914","pages":"178-198","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"CPP 2021: Proceedings of the 10th ACM SIGPLAN International Conference on Certified Programs and Proofs"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85100539579"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-618f45a0-50de-43b2-a610-fe8b52212bdd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Machine-Checked Semantic Session Typing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382729","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Hazard evaluation of graphene-based materials (GBM) is still in its early stage and it is slowed by their large diversity in the physicochemical properties. This study explores transcriptomic differences in the lung and liver after pulmonary exposure to two GBM with similar physical properties, but different surface chemistry. Female C57BL/6 mice were exposed by a single intratracheal instillation of 0, 18, 54 or 162 μg/mouse of graphene oxide (GO) or reduced graphene oxide (rGO). Pulmonary and hepatic changes in the transcriptome were profiled to identify commonly and uniquely perturbed functions and pathways by GO and rGO. These changes were then related to previously analyzed toxicity endpoints. GO exposure induced more differentially expressed genes, affected more functions, and perturbed more pathways compared to rGO, both in lung and liver tissues. The largest differences were observed for the pulmonary innate immune response and acute phase response, and for hepatic lipid homeostasis, which were strongly induced after GO exposure. These changes collective indicate a potential for atherosclerotic changes after GO, but not rGO exposure. As GO and rGO are physically similar, the higher level of hydroxyl groups on the surface of GO is likely the main reason for the observed differences. GO exposure also uniquely induced changes in the transcriptome related to fibrosis, whereas both GBM induced similar changes related to Reactive Oxygen Species production and genotoxicity. The differences in transcriptomic responses between the two GBM types can be used to understand how physicochemical properties influence biological responses and enable hazard evaluation of GBM and hazard ranking of GO and rGO, both in relation to each other and to other nanomaterials.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Poulsen, Sarah S.","Bengtson, Stefan","Williams, Andrew","Jacobsen, Nicklas R.","Troelsen, Jesper T.","Halappanavar, Sabina","Vogel, Ulla Birgitte"],"cuid":["S03-097.81-768430"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Vogel, Ulla Birgitte"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Environmental and Radiation Health Sciences Directorate, Health Canada , Ottawa, Canada.","Health Canada","Health Canada, Ottawa"],"keyword":["Acute phase response","DNA microarray","In vivo","Inflammation","Kemisk arbejdsmiljø","Nano","Nanotoxicology","Partikler","Toxicogenomics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a transcriptomic overview of lung and liver changes one day after pulmonary exposure to graphene and graphene oxide","src":["dtu","nfa","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.taap.2020.115343","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-097.81-768430","identifier":[{"id":"33227293","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85097246118","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-bd7e962b-bd64-4675-9eba-564e4c9a764f","nfa-9973d588-ab80-45ed-848f-4bce366c15b4","ruc-6750b25a-80f7-416f-a6fe-730b3265b849"],"keyword":["Acute phase response","DNA microarray","In vivo","Inflammation","Kemisk arbejdsmiljø","Nano","Nanotoxicology","Partikler","Toxicogenomics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-2EA6EFAD5FF80846BDCF8498EB16CEAF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/235411543/1_s2.0_S0041008X20304658_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/74809751/1_s2.0_S0041008X20304658_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.taap.2020.115343","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Chemical Working Environment, Toxicology, Nanosafety, and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"health canada","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Health Canada","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"health canada ottawa","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Health Canada, Ottawa","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"ca","key":"environmental and radiation health sciences directorate health canada ottawa canada","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Environmental and Radiation Health Sciences Directorate, Health Canada, Ottawa, Canada.","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah S","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Sarah S","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Stefan","key":"bengtsonpau","last":"Bengtson","locid":"b39e999d-f0c0-4cb3-bb6b-2f4c31ed7f82","name":"Bengtson, Stefan","orcid":"0000-0001-6174-2161","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew","key":"williamspau","last":"Williams","name":"Williams, Andrew","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicklas R","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"2767126a-8d1d-42ef-a04e-a9f126721bbe","name":"Jacobsen, Nicklas Raun","name_org":"Jacobsen, Nicklas R","orcid":"0000-0002-2504-2229","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Jesper Thorvald","key":"troelsenpau","last":"Troelsen","locid":"3b39117d-6f4e-47c7-a61d-5192c15b00a9","name":"Troelsen, Jesper","name_org":"Troelsen, Jesper Thorvald","orcid":"0000-0002-4177-3267","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Sabina","key":"halappanavarpau","last":"Halappanavar","name":"Halappanavar, Sabina","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulla Birgitte","key":"vogelpau","last":"Vogel","locid":"b09b3c47-5cc7-474a-af05-a4b378c96531","name":"Vogel, Ulla Birgitte","orcid":"0000-0001-6807-1524","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33227293"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.taap.2020.115343","issn":["0041008X","10960333"],"issn_org":["0041008X"],"journal":"Toxicology and Applied Pharmacology","pages":"115343","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Toxicology and Applied Pharmacology","volume":"410"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85097246118"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Roskilde University","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-bd7e962b-bd64-4675-9eba-564e4c9a764f","nfa-9973d588-ab80-45ed-848f-4bce366c15b4","ruc-6750b25a-80f7-416f-a6fe-730b3265b849"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"A transcriptomic overview of lung and liver changes one day after pulmonary exposure to graphene and graphene oxide","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-097.81-768430","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Message passing is a useful abstraction to implement concurrent programs. For real-world systems, however, it is often combined with other programming and concurrency paradigms, such as higher-order functions, mutable state, shared-memory concurrency, and locks. We present Actris: a logic for proving functional correctness of programs that use a combination of the aforementioned features. Actris combines the power of modern concurrent separation logics with a first-class protocol mechanism—based on session types—for reasoning about message passing in the presence of other concurrency paradigms. We show that Actris provides a suitable level of abstraction by proving functional correctness of a variety of examples, including a distributed merge sort, a distributed load-balancing mapper, and a variant of the map-reduce model, using relatively simple specifications. Soundness of Actris is proved using a model of its protocol mechanism in the Iris framework. We mechanised the theory of Actris, together with tactics for symbolic execution of programs, as well as all examples in the paper, in the Coq proof assistant","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hinrichsen, Jonas Kastberg","Bengtson, Jesper","Krebbers, Robbert"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382334"],"event":{"acronym":"POPL","title":"ACM SIGPLAN Symposium on Principles of Programming Languages"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology"],"keyword":["Functional Correctness","Message passing","Session types","concurrent programming","separation logics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"actris session type based reasoning in separation logic","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3371074","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382334","identifier":[{"id":"85079453170","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-475db6ac-7a50-4f01-8c05-1a7e17de8d63"],"keyword":["concurrent programming","functional correctness","message passing","separation logics","session types"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C4DEE961277F325C1AECC9684ADD8CCE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3371074","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85391057/3371074.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Delft University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Kastberg","key":"hinrichsenpau","last":"Hinrichsen","name":"Hinrichsen, Jonas Kastberg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"bengtsonpau","last":"Bengtson","locid":"b2b68ce2-6257-45bf-ab48-dc17d05c885e","name":"Bengtson, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Robbert","key":"krebberspau","last":"Krebbers","name":"Krebbers, Robbert","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Philip","key":"wadlerpedh","last":"Wadler","name":"Wadler, Philip","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3371074","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079453170"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-475db6ac-7a50-4f01-8c05-1a7e17de8d63"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Actris: session-type based reasoning in separation logic","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382334","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"A series of Gs protein peptidomimetics were designed and synthesised based on the published X-ray crystal structure of the active state β2-Adrenergic receptor (β2AR) in complex with the Gs protein (PDB 3SN6). We hypothesised that such peptidomimetics may function as allosteric modulators that target the intracellular Gs protein binding site of the β2AR. Peptidomimetics were designed to mimic the 15 residue C-Terminal α-helix of the Gs protein and were pre-organised in a helical conformation by (i, i + 4)-stapling using copper catalysed azide alkyne cycloaddition. Linear and stapled peptidomimetics were analysed by circular dichroism (CD) and characterised in a membrane-based cAMP accumulation assay and in a bimane fluorescence assay on purified β2AR. Several peptidomimetics inhibited agonist isoproterenol (ISO) induced cAMP formation by lowering the ISO maximal efficacy up to 61%. Moreover, some peptidomimetics were found to significantly decrease the potency of ISO up to 39-fold. In the bimane fluorescence assay none of the tested peptidomimetics could stabilise an active-like conformation of β2AR. Overall, the obtained pharmacological data suggest that some of the peptidomimetics may be able to compete with the native Gs protein for the intracellular binding site to block ISO-induced cAMP formation, but are unable to stabilise an active-like receptor conformation.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Boyhus, Lotte Emilie","Danielsen, Mia","Bengtson, Nina Smidt","Kunze, Micha Ben Achim","Kubiak, Xavier Jean Philippe","Sminia, Tjerk J.","Løper, Jacob Hartvig","Tran, Phuong Thu","Lindorff-Larsen, Kresten","Rasmussen, Søren Gøgsig Faarup","Mathiesen, Jesper M.","Pedersen, Daniel Sejer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-465025"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"g sub s sub protein peptidomimetics as allosteric modulators of the β sub 000000000002 sub adrenergic receptor","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/c7ra11713b","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-465025","identifier":[{"id":"85040919810","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-779a451a-aab3-4268-9abd-4cded6482c94"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E954F25734D2B66B73F9FDBA64949485"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/204118470/c7ra11713b.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/c7ra11713b","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Medicinal Chemistry Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lotte Emilie","key":"boyhuspau","last":"Boyhus","locid":"786bbead-8072-4884-ac9a-acab8f366054","name":"Boyhus, Lotte Emilie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mia","key":"danielsenpau","last":"Danielsen","locid":"41ae2ebe-0eaa-4607-a3c2-fba848d13a56","name":"Danielsen, Mia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nina Smidt","key":"bengtsonpau","last":"Bengtson","name":"Bengtson, Nina Smidt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Micha Ben Achim","key":"kunzepau","last":"Kunze","locid":"5b3f23af-a162-4383-bc5d-c8c9264363c5","name":"Kunze, Micha Ben Achim","orcid":"0000-0001-8922-5510","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xavier","key":"kubiakpau","last":"Kubiak","locid":"acf2152e-59a5-4dfb-b2e3-a04492c43a37","name":"Kubiak, Xavier Jean Philippe","name_org":"Kubiak, Xavier","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tjerk J.","key":"sminiapau","last":"Sminia","name":"Sminia, Tjerk J.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob Hartvig","key":"løperpau","last":"Løper","name":"Løper, Jacob Hartvig","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Phuong Thu","key":"tranpau","last":"Tran","locid":"4df14aad-8413-4648-86bf-008599e98e54","name":"Tran, Phuong Thu","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kresten","key":"lindorfflarsenpau","last":"Lindorff-Larsen","locid":"be20a4d8-92c4-44b9-9dfb-b6ad6471a58c","name":"Lindorff-Larsen, Kresten","orcid":"0000-0002-4750-6039","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren G.F.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"916c4655-dd61-4f65-a56a-d19ed9efb5f4","name":"Rasmussen, Søren Gøgsig Faarup","name_org":"Rasmussen, Søren G.F.","orcid":"0000-0002-1853-1841","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper Mosolff","key":"mathiesenpau","last":"Mathiesen","locid":"56a28f89-7748-48e3-8ad8-383d67ef351b","name":"Mathiesen, Jesper M.","name_org":"Mathiesen, Jesper Mosolff","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Daniel Sejer","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5dc5469d-7fb0-40c3-81bc-d7666a18e27d","name":"Pedersen, Daniel Sejer","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/c7ra11713b","issn":["20462069"],"issue":"4","journal":"RSC Advances","pages":"2219-2228","status":"p","title":"RSC Advances","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85040919810"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-779a451a-aab3-4268-9abd-4cded6482c94"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"G<sub>s</sub> protein peptidomimetics as allosteric modulators of the β<sub>2</sub>-adrenergic receptor","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-465025","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"We investigated toxicity of 2-3 layered >1 μm sized graphene oxide (GO) and reduced graphene oxide (rGO) in mice following single intratracheal exposure with respect to pulmonary inflammation, acute phase response (biomarker for risk of cardiovascular disease) and genotoxicity. In addition, we assessed exposure levels of particulate matter emitted during production of graphene in a clean room and in a normal industrial environment using chemical vapour deposition. Toxicity was evaluated at day 1, 3, 28 and 90 days (18, 54 and 162 μg/mouse), except for GO exposed mice at day 28 and 90 where only the lowest dose was evaluated. GO induced a strong acute inflammatory response together with a pulmonary (Serum-Amyloid A, Saa3) and hepatic (Saa1) acute phase response. rGO induced less acute, but a constant and prolonged inflammation up to day 90. Lung histopathology showed particle agglomerates at day 90 without signs of fibrosis. In addition, DNA damage in BAL cells was observed across time points and doses for both GO and rGO. In conclusion, pulmonary exposure to GO and rGO induced inflammation, acute phase response and genotoxicity but no fibrosis.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Bengtson, Stefan","Knudsen, Kristina Bram","Kyjovska, Zdenka O.","Berthing, Trine","Skaug, Vidar","Levin, Marcus","Koponen, Ismo K.","Shivayogimath, Abhay","Booth, Tim","Alonso, Beatriz","Pesquera, Amaia","Zurutuza, Amaia","Thomsen, Birthe L.","Troelsen, Jesper T.","Jacobsen, Nicklas R.","Vogel, Ulla Birgitte"],"cuid":["S03-098.78-768422"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Graphenea","National Institute of Occupational Health","National Institute of Occupational Health (STAMI), Oslo, Norway."],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"OT":["R&D Department, Graphenea S.A., San Sebastian, Spain."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"differences in inflammation and acute phase response but similar genotoxicity in mice following pulmonary exposure to graphene oxide and reduced graphene oxide","src":["dtu","nfa","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0178355","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-098.78-768422","identifier":[{"id":"28570647","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5453440","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85019970216","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ba70bf74-36dd-47a8-a1cb-97438e92e246","nfa-7118a4d8-f360-4916-ae8e-78cea02909e7","ruc-498db209-be00-4b38-afc3-e8342dc8dec1"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-A6373F802DDCA733F8199AC5176E0B14"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/133054344/journal.pone.0178355.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/59944949/journal.pone.0178355.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0178355","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC