:"Thomsen, Birthe L","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"troelsenpau","last":"Troelsen","locid":"3b39117d-6f4e-47c7-a61d-5192c15b00a9","name":"Troelsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-4177-3267","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicklas R","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"2767126a-8d1d-42ef-a04e-a9f126721bbe","name":"Jacobsen, Nicklas Raun","name_org":"Jacobsen, Nicklas R","orcid":"0000-0002-2504-2229","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla","key":"vogelpau","last":"Vogel","locid":"157e7e7e-7506-4f84-8087-ccc586d5d13c","name":"Vogel, Ulla Birgitte","name_org":"Vogel, Ulla","orcid":"0000-0001-6807-1524","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28570647"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0178355","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"6","journal":"PLOS ONE","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019970216"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Roskilde University","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ba70bf74-36dd-47a8-a1cb-97438e92e246","nfa-7118a4d8-f360-4916-ae8e-78cea02909e7","ruc-498db209-be00-4b38-afc3-e8342dc8dec1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Differences in inflammation and acute phase response but similar genotoxicity in mice following pulmonary exposure to graphene oxide and reduced graphene oxide","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-098.78-768422","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Foundational proof assistants simultaneously offer both expressive logics and strong guarantees. The price they pay for this flexibility is often the need to build and check explicit proof objects which can be expensive. In this work we develop a collection of techniques for building reflective automation, where proofs are witnessed by verified decision procedures rather than verbose proof objects. Our techniques center around a verified domain specific language for proving, Rtac, written in Gallina, Coq’s logic. The design of tactics makes it easy to combine them into higher-level automation that can be proved sound in a mostly automated way. Furthermore, unlike traditional uses of reflection, Rtac tactics are independent of the underlying problem domain. This allows them to be re-tasked to automate new problems with very little effort. We demonstrate the usability of Rtac through several case studies demonstrating orders of magnitude speedups for relatively little engineering work.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Malecha, Gregory","Bengtson, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381829"],"event":{"acronym":"ESOP","end":"2016-04-07","place":"Eindhoven, nl","start":"2016-04-02","title":"European Symposium on Programming","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of California"],"keyword":["Coq","Interactive proof assistants","Proof by reflection"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extensible and efficient automation through reflective tactics","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81631209/rtac_esop16.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-381829","identifier":[{"id":"84961684143","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-254931ea-319e-446e-840f-5890104cf19f"],"keyword":["Coq","Interactive proof assistants","Proof by reflection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-D3170728E0F88A412C2927163CC330DC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81631209/rtac_esop16.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of california","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gregory","key":"malechapau","last":"Malecha","name":"Malecha, Gregory","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"bengtsonpau","last":"Bengtson","locid":"b2b68ce2-6257-45bf-ab48-dc17d05c885e","name":"Bengtson, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-49498-1_21","eisbn":["9783662494981"],"isbn":["9783662494974"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"532-559","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"25th European Symposium on Programming, ESOP 2016, Held as Part of the European Joint Conferences on Theory and Practice of Software, ETAPS 2016, Eindhoven, The Netherlands, April 2–8, 2016, Proceedings","title":"Programming Languages and Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84961684143"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-254931ea-319e-446e-840f-5890104cf19f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Extensible and Efficient Automation Through Reflective Tactics","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381829","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"User interfaces for interactive proof assistants have always lagged behind those for mainstream programming languages. Whereas integrated development environments—IDEs—have support for features like project management, version control, dependency analysis and incremental project compilation, “IDE”s for proof assistants typically only operate on files in isolation, relying on external tools to integrate those files into larger projects. In this paper we present Coqoon, an IDE for Coq developments integrated into Eclipse. Coqoon manages proofs as projects rather than isolated source files, and compiles these projects using the Eclipse common build system. Coqoon takes advantage of the latest features of Coq, including asynchronous and parallel processing of proofs, and—when used together with a third-party OCaml extension for Eclipse—can even be used to work on large developments containing Coq plugins.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Faithfull, Alexander","Bengtson, Jesper","Tassi, Enrico"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382869"],"event":{"acronym":"TACAS","end":"2016-04-07","place":"Eindhoven, nl","start":"2016-04-02","title":"Tools and Algorithms for the Construction and Analysis of Systems","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The French National Institute for Computer Science (INRIA)"],"keyword":["Coq","Eclipse","IDEs","Proof assistants"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coqoon an ide for interactive proof development in coq","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81631129/main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382869","identifier":[{"id":"84964059464","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6b9ab6df-a5d3-4612-9118-048708e55ab6"],"keyword":["Coq","Eclipse","IDEs","Proof assistants"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B50EBAD86693E1F5CB04E3C3D14A404F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81631129/main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"the french national institute for computer science","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"The French National Institute for Computer Science (INRIA)","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"faithfullpau","last":"Faithfull","name":"Faithfull, Alexander","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"bengtsonpau","last":"Bengtson","locid":"b2b68ce2-6257-45bf-ab48-dc17d05c885e","name":"Bengtson, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Enrico","key":"tassipau","last":"Tassi","name":"Tassi, Enrico","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-49674-9_18","eisbn":["9783662496749"],"isbn":["9783662496732"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"316-331","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"TACAS 2016: Tools and Algorithms for the Construction and Analysis of Systems","title":"22nd International Conference, TACAS 2016, Held as Part of the European Joint Conferences on Theory and Practice of Software, ETAPS 2016, Eindhoven, The Netherlands, April 2-8, 2016, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84964059464"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6b9ab6df-a5d3-4612-9118-048708e55ab6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Coqoon - An IDE for Interactive Proof Development in Coq","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382869","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a mechanisation of psi-calculi, a parametric framework for modelling various dialects of process calculi including (but not limited to) the pi-calculus, the applied pi-calculus, and the spi calculus. Psi-calculi are significantly more expressive, yet their semantics is as simple in structure as the semantics of the original pi-calculus. Proofs of meta-theoretic properties for psi-calculi are more involved, however, not least because psi-calculi (unlike simpler calculi) utilise binders that bind multiple names at once. The mechanisation is carried out in the Nominal Isabelle framework, an interactive proof assistant designed to facilitate formal reasoning about calculi with binders. Our main contributions are twofold. First, we have developed techniques that allow efficient reasoning about calculi that bind multiple names in Nominal Isabelle. Second, we have adopted these techniques to mechanise substantial results from the meta-theory of psi-calculi, including congruence properties of bisimilarity and the laws of structural congruence. To our knowledge, this is the most extensive formalisation of process calculi mechanised in a proof assistant to date.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bengtson, Jesper","Parrow, Joachim","Weber, Tjark"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381678"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Interactive proof assistants","Isabelle","Process calculi"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"psi calculi in isabelle","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81625644/psiIsabelleLong.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381678","identifier":[{"id":"84953638582","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1b8c5c18-acc0-4241-b6f5-1d281f1fffac"],"keyword":["Interactive proof assistants","Isabelle","Process calculi"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A8FF055253A3B899DF2F56211C9F501A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81625644/psiIsabelleLong.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"bengtsonpau","last":"Bengtson","locid":"b2b68ce2-6257-45bf-ab48-dc17d05c885e","name":"Bengtson, Jesper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Joachim","key":"parrowpau","last":"Parrow","name":"Parrow, Joachim","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tjark","key":"weberpau","last":"Weber","name":"Weber, Tjark","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10817-015-9336-2","issn":["01687433","15730670"],"issn_org":["01687433"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Automated Reasoning","pages":"1-47","paperid":"1","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of Automated Reasoning","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84953638582"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1b8c5c18-acc0-4241-b6f5-1d281f1fffac"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Psi-calculi in Isabelle","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381678","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Oxaliplatin resistance in colorectal cancers (CRC) is a major medical problem, and predictive markers are urgently needed. Recently, miR-625-3p was reported as a promising predictive marker. Herein, we show that miR-625-3p functionally induces oxaliplatin resistance in CRC cells, and identify the signalling networks affected by miR-625-3p. We show that the p38 MAPK activator MAP2K6 is a direct target of miR-625-3p, and, accordingly, is downregulated in non-responder patients of oxaliplatin therapy. miR-625-3p-mediated resistance is reversed by anti-miR-625-3p treatment and ectopic expression of a miR-625-3p insensitive MAP2K6 variant. In addition, reduction of p38 signalling by using siRNAs, chemical inhibitors or expression of a dominant-negative MAP2K6 protein induces resistance to oxaliplatin. Transcriptome, proteome and phosphoproteome profiles confirm inactivation of MAP2K6-p38 signalling as one likely mechanism of oxaliplatin resistance. Our study shows that miR-625-3p induces oxaliplatin resistance by abrogating MAP2K6-p38-regulated apoptosis and cell cycle control networks, and corroborates the predictive power of miR-625-3p.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Mads Heilskov","Lyskjær, Iben","Jersie-Christensen, Rosa Rakownikow","Tarpgaard, Line Schmidt","Primdal-Bengtson, Bjarke","Nielsen, Morten Muhlig","Pedersen, Jakob Skou","Hansen, Tine Plato","Hansen, Flemming","Olsen, Jesper Velgaard","Pfeiffer, Per","Ørntoft, Torben Falck","Andersen, Claus Lindbjerg"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-013509"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"